// Title: Office Macros Warning Disabled
// Sigma ID: 91239011-fe3c-4b54-9f24-15c86bb65913
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Trent Liffick (@tliffick), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-05-22 | Modified: 2024-03-19
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects registry changes to Microsoft Office "VBAWarning" to a value of "1" which enables the
//   execution of all macros, whether signed or unsigned.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/inversecos/status/1494174785621819397
//   - https://www.mcafee.com/blogs/other-blogs/mcafee-labs/zloader-with-a-new-infection-technique/
//   - https://securelist.com/scarcruft-surveilling-north-korean-defectors-and-human-rights-activists/105074/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_office_vba_warnings_tamper.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Security\\VBAWarnings" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
